# search-demo scope 100 — /find?q=…: what anyone may see.
#
# `query` is plain language. A quoted string is a phrase, an identifier such
# as TXC-4821 is matched whole, and everything else is OR-ed and ranked, so a
# whole sentence works as a query. No engine syntax is recognised.
#
# `filter` is the grammar txco://vector/search takes, so one filter object can
# narrow both retrieval lanes. It admits or rejects; it never moves the order.
# Hits land at `into` (default `_search.hits`), best first:
# [{id, rank, text, metadata}]. There is no score.
WHEN @src == "http" && @web.req.url.path == "/find"
  && @web.req.url.query.q.0 != "" && @web.req.url.query.as.0 != "team"
  EXEC "txco://search/query"
    WITH collection = "handbook",
         query = @web.req.url.query.q.0,
         limit = 5,
         filter = &object("audience", "anyone")
